    "function": "read_export",
    "issue": "Path containment is checked with a fragile string-prefix test (str(target).startswith(str(root))) and absolute names are never rejected. A sibling directory whose path string shares the root prefix (e.g. ../exports_secret) and symlinks resolving outside root both bypass the check, and an absolute name is accepted, violating the required PermissionError for any resolved path outside root, absolute names, and external symlinks.",
    "reproduction": "repro.py check_read_export_traversal: on the original service reads ../exports_secret/secret.txt ('TOPSECRET'), reads an external symlink pointing outside root ('TARGET'), and reads via absolute name '/ok.txt'; the repair using relative_to(root) and an is_absolute() guard raises PermissionError for all three, failing the assertions."
  }
]

